    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0640" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/1–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-30T16:00:00-05:00">January 30, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. Urtel 515 rptd London as 61.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d387-f1"/> Dept increasingly concerned by atmosphere of crisis
                    prevailing in Paris and its disintegrating effects on coalition. Your talk with
                    Blum approved. Do not hesitate approach Blum again or other leaders whose
                    parties show signs of bolting whenever you feel this action would be
                    salutary.</p>
                <p>Gallman may wish indicate in proper quarters our concern lest things get out of
                    hand in Paris at this time.</p>
                <p>Sent Paris as 297; rptd London as 317.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
